+# START HERE - Slop Game Lab
+
+A working research library for an **original, colorful, meme-friendly Roblox collection game**. “AI slop” describes the intended fast, absurd aesthetic here—not an excuse for broken purchases, copied assets, or an unplayable loop.
+
+## Best first path
+1. [[Original Game Direction and MVP Contract]] — choose the distinctive loop.
+2. [[Colorful UI Production Brief]] — use the supplied screenshot as mood, then build original UI.
+3. [[Monetization Catalog and Grant Map]] — a broad optional-product catalog with one reliable fulfilment system.
+4. [[MVP Build Board]] — implement small verified slices.
+5. [[Robot Prompt Library]] — paste a bounded task into the coding robot.
+
+## Knowledge clusters
+- [[MOC - Core Design]]
+- [[MOC - Systems]]
+- [[MOC - Colorful UI]]
+- [[MOC - Economy]]
+- [[MOC - Monetization]]
+- [[MOC - Art and Content]]
+- [[MOC - AI Workflow]]
+- [[MOC - Growth and Analytics]]
+- [[MOC - LiveOps]]
+- [[MOC - QA and Release]]
+
+## Research and navigation
+- [[Reference Library]] — source records and inherited links with review labels.
+- [[Video Review Desk]] — three timestamped transcript reviews, not a claim of full video playback.
+- [[Concept Incubator]] — original alternative hooks; none is a proven commercial winner.
+- [[Research Methods and Evidence Ledger]] — what is verified, inferred, proposed, and still open.
+- [[Graph View and Vault Guide]] — see the linked graph and navigate without any add-on.
+- [[Economy Model and Worked Examples]] — draft arithmetic, model checks, and boundaries.
+- [[First Playtest Protocol]] — observations that decide what to build next.
+
+## Operating rule
+Read a source, write a decision, implement a small slice, test an invariant, and update the note. A dense graph should reflect real relationships—not hundreds of empty files or claims that a YouTube success story guarantees results.
